## Setup

Install [Homebrew](https://brew.sh), then run in the repository:

```sh
brew bundle                                   # mise and the GitHub CLI
mise trust && mise install                    # cabal, ghcup, Ormolu, cabal-gild, HLint
mise exec -- ghcup install ghc {{ghc_version}}
mise exec -- ghcup install hls 2.15.0.0       # editor support
mise exec -- cabal update
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
gh extension install github/gh-stack          # optional: stacked PRs
```

`mise.toml` pins every tool except GHC, and `mise.lock` holds their checksums. ghcup installs GHC
and HLS into `~/.ghcup/bin`. `with-compiler` in `cabal.project` names the GHC version, so cabal,
HLS, `scripts/check` and CI all use the same one. `scripts/check` accepts only ghcup's GHC: another
build of the same version rebuilds every dependency.

Copies of GHC, cabal, Ormolu or HLint from Homebrew may stay installed. The scripts and the
commands below run the pinned versions through mise. The git hook runs the checks before each
push. `gh stack` is optional: it helps to open and update stacked PRs.

## Commands

```sh
scripts/check        # every quality gate: format, lint, lock, build, test
scripts/format       # format the .hs and .cabal files
scripts/freeze       # after a dependency change: re-lock the versions
mise exec -- cabal build all
mise exec -- cabal test all
mise exec -- cabal repl lib:{{package}}
mise exec -- cabal install --enable-optimization   # release build: cabal.project builds with -O0
```

`scripts/check` is the single list of gates. The git hook and CI run it too. A weekly CI job,
`.github/workflows/scheduled.yml`, tries random QuickCheck seeds and reports newer dependency
versions. It never blocks a merge.

